        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF150 added support for  <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/customElementRegistry\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Element.customElementRegistry</code></a>, <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/customElementRegistry\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Document.customElementRegistry</code></a> <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ShadowRoot/customElementRegistry\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">ShadowRoot.customElementRegistry</code></a> behind the preference <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.scoped-custom-element-registries.enabled</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the experimental features page update and corresponding link from FF150 release note page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127730538\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43555\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43555/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43555\">#43555</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43592",
            "title": "FF150 ExprFeat: customElementRegistry on Document, Element, ShadowRoot",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T04:50:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-27T04:48:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF150 supports <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/caretRangeFromPoint\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\"> Document.caretRangeFromPoint()</code></a>. This is non-standard, so primarily for parity reasons.<br>\nDevelopers should prefer <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/caretPositionFromPoint\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">caretPositionFromPoint()</code></a> when supported \"generally\" because it is shadow root aware (but not on FF, which doesn't support the option according to BCD).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note, and also updates the docs to explain why you should prefer <code class=\"notranslate\">caretPositionFromPoint()</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127666989\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43550\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43550/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43550\">#43550</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43591",
            "title": "FF150Relnote: Document.caretRangeFromPoint() supported",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T13:45:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-27T03:44:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR addresses the dev-docs-needed requirements of:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2022549\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 2022549</a> tabs.move() taking a list of tabs should unsplit a split view when its tabs are explicitly listed apart</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2016751\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 2016751</a> tabs.move() does not move a tab to the specified index when the destination is part of a split view</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In addition, it adds a section summarizing the features for working with groups and split views in the working with the tab API article.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43589",
            "title": "Release 150 tab split view functionality",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T01:05:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T18:17:33.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the “How to sunset a section of content” guide.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To describe the process for retiring entire sections of MDN Web Docs content.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43588",
            "title": "Add Sunsetting content guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T16:43:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T17:01:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pepelsbey",
                "url": "https://github.com/pepelsbey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">adding a new guide.<br>\nOther guide is <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3838773711\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42853\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42853/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42853\">#42853</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43587",
            "title": "New guide: animation timeline range insets",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T15:39:49.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T15:27:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds reference docs for WebAssembly SIMD arithmetic instructions (and possibly some more bitwise ones too).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note: I've updated the general <code class=\"notranslate\">shl</code> page to cover SIMD and non-SIMD values. I've also deleted the previously published SIMD-specific <code class=\"notranslate\">shl</code> page and redirected it to the general one.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43583",
            "title": "Document Wasm SIMD arithmetic instructions",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-26T17:53:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T11:55:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56009637?u=2c59626cda2ec34a16e55d6071ceaffb1698a34a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Applies the css invert to the item in the example labelled <code class=\"notranslate\">invert() filter</code> instead of the SVG invert for the <code class=\"notranslate\">SVG filter equivalent</code>, and fixes the SVG filter equivalent with a class as the document's text explains rather than as an inline SVG.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The changes keep the content accurate and make the playground more useable.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43581",
            "title": "Changes example in CSS invert() to use appropriate classes.",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-26T20:57:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T02:25:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "elooly10",
                "url": "https://github.com/elooly10"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add links to the SUMO user documentation for split view mentions.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To provide more information for developers unfamiliar with the split view feature.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a follow up to <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43284\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43284/hovercard\">Bug-1993037 addition of splitViewId to the tabs API</a> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4001919102\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43284\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43284/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43284\">#43284</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43576",
            "title": "Cross-link to the user guide on split view",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-25T22:36:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-25T16:35:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Between versions 142 and 145, Chrome enables support for various features of the <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Local Network Access spec</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928</a> and <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically, these are:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">targetAddressSpace</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">Request</code> property, and the equivalent <code class=\"notranslate\">RequestInit</code> property.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network-access</code> permission/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directive.</li>\n<li>The more granular <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">loopback-network</code> permissions/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directives.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adds reference pages for the above features.</li>\n<li>Adds a new \"Local network access\" guide inside the MDN security section (I didn't add a regular API page for this, because it doesn't really feel like it warrants an API page — it is just a single property and some new permissions, in terms of web developer footprint.)</li>\n<li>Adds links to the guide from several related places.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43575",
            "title": "Technical review: Document local network access",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T14:03:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-25T15:14:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">the value is in the spec.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/scroll-animations/#typedef-timeline-range-name\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://drafts.csswg.org/scroll-animations/#typedef-timeline-range-name</a></p>",
